(20191, 484, 'message', 'Saalam alaykom, \n1. I have a question regarding the sharia-compliance of your products. Your ads only mention the expected return from the investment, but doesn\'t mention anything about the possible rate of loss in case the project fails for whatever reason. In fact, your ads mention that there are guaranties such as post dated cheques from the project developer.\nI am not an expert in sharia-compliance, but to my knowledge, a Halal investment means that the investors have a share of possible gains and possible losses from the investment. If the amount of investment is guaranteed with a post date cheque as you describe, isn\'t that similar to interest-based loans, where the bank secure the loans via collaterals ?\nPlease explain this important issue.\n2. You have been working for few years but haven\'t been certified as sharia-compliant until now by any official institution ... why is that ?\nThank you,\nRachid', '2025-12-18 08:21:55', '2025-12-18 08:21:55'),
